 considered gold medal favourites."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The big question of the 2002 Olympic luge doubles concerned whether the home track advantage of the American pairs would be enough to topple the Europeans and earn a first US Olympic gold in the sport. The answer was to be no but the margin of victory for the German pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/101508"} "Alexander Resch"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/101507"} "Patric Leitner"] " was small.\nResch and Leitner, the 2004 world champions, set the best time of the first run with " [:a {:href "/athletes/87410"} "Clay Ives"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/98254"} "Chris Thorpe"] " leading US teammates, the " [:a {:href "/athletes/86232"} "Mark Grimmette"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/100476"} "Brian Martin"] " combination, for second and third. The Americans were both faster than the German leaders over the final run but not by enough to overhaul them for the gold medal. Grimmette and Martin were fast enough to put themselves ahead of their compatriots and into the silver medal position."] "\n\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/101508"} "Alexander Resch"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/101507"} "Patric Leitner"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "1:26.082"] [:td {} "42.953 (1)"] [:td {} "43.129 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/100476"} "Brian Martin"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/86232"} "Mark Grimmette"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-centra